On my nice (Pentium M) laptop:

Using no optimization, I got "3 2".
Using -O3 -march=pentium3, I got "3 2".
Using -O3 -march=pentium3 -frename-registers, I got "2 2".
Using -O3 -march=pentium4 -frename-registers, I sometimes got sigbus and
sometimes "3 3", if the machine was loaded. If it was idle I always got
sigbus. *Ouch*.

(FYI, the Pentium M has all the opcodes of a P4, but scheduling is most
efficient if done like a P3 - it's a *sibling* of P4, not a descendant. I
have to tell GCC about those opcodes, though; I didn't here, but I don't
really think SSE2 support changes things much.)

In conclusion, the behaviour is very undefined indeed.


